## Answers to Your Key Questions

### 1. Do we need a separate web frontend?

**Yes.** You'll create a third folder `admin/` alongside `backend/` and `mobile/`. This will be a **React web app** (using Vite) that runs in the browser. Your project structure becomes:

```
Ceylon-boutique/
├── backend/      # Node.js + Express REST API (existing)
├── mobile/       # Expo React Native app (existing)
└── admin/        # React + Vite Admin Web Panel (NEW)
```

### 2. Can all three run together locally?

**Yes, absolutely.** Here's how:

| App | Port | URL |
|-----|------|-----|
| Backend API | 5000 | `http://localhost:5000` |
| Admin Web | 5173 (Vite default) | `http://localhost:5173` |
| Mobile App | Expo Go | Via QR code on your phone |

All three connect to the **same backend** on port 5000, which connects to the **same MongoDB Atlas** database. The admin web runs on `localhost` (not a mobile IP) so it can use `http://localhost:5000` directly.

> [!NOTE]
> The mobile app uses your machine's IP (e.g., `192.168.x.x:5000`) because phones can't resolve `localhost`. The admin web panel runs on your computer's browser, so it **can** use `localhost:5000`.

### 3. Can we reuse the existing login system for admin?

**Yes — with a separate admin login page.** Your User model already has `role: 'admin'`. The admin web will:
1. Have its own login page (separate from mobile)
2. Call a **new** `/api/admin/login` endpoint (which checks `role === 'admin'`)
3. Use the **same JWT system** — same `protect` middleware, same `authorize('admin')` checks
4. Store the token in browser `localStorage` (like mobile uses `AsyncStorage`)

We'll also create a **seed script** to insert the first admin account into the database, since admins can't self-register.

