### Component 3: CORS & Connectivity Configuration

#### [MODIFY] [server.js](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/Ceylon-boutique/backend/server.js)

Update CORS config to accept multiple origins:

```js
const allowedOrigins = [
  'http://localhost:5173',  // Admin web (Vite dev)
  'http://localhost:3000',  // Admin web (alternative)
  process.env.ADMIN_WEB_URL,
].filter(Boolean);

app.use(cors({
  origin: process.env.CORS_ORIGIN === '*' ? '*' : allowedOrigins,
  methods: ['GET', 'POST', 'PUT', 'DELETE'],
  allowedHeaders: ['Content-Type', 'Authorization'],
  credentials: true,
}));
```

> [!TIP]
> During local development, `CORS_ORIGIN=*` (already your default) allows all origins. In production, set it to your specific domains.

